            <note type="project" target="#dat1">This manuscript was probably composed between 22 March and 10 May 1890, since the letter on the reverse bears the former date and a later draft of the poem (loc.00239) bears a note indicating that it was written on the latter date.</note>                
            <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.0383" cert="high">"On, On the Same, Ye Jocund Twain!" was first published in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi>, in May 1891. It also appeared shortly thereafter in the 9 June 1891 issue of the magazine <hi rend="italic">Once a Week</hi>.</note>                        	
